-- #423: the planned nodes the smaller farms move, re-planned (plots plan
-- §5.3). The rural ring's woods, branches, outcrops and veins keep off the
-- farms and the lanes, and the farms are laid differently now, so the rural
-- plan changes. The wilds' branches and old growth are planned after it on
-- the same spacing grid, by rejection sampling, so they move too (as at R7,
-- #340). The veins in the ranges, the reeds, the clay and the stone, and the
-- city's and the suburb's nodes keep their rows.
--
-- So this deletes the rows the plan no longer has, by id, and inserts the new
-- ones, as 20261126_001_rural_farms_nodes.sql did. Nothing a player owns is a
-- node; a node half gathered starts over. The woods cover the ring a little
-- differently with the farms in it: 954 trees are 955.
--
-- The rows come from the ignored test `print_node_replan`, and
-- `the_migration_writes_the_default_plan` checks the plan still matches.
--
-- 8395 deleted: {("fallen_branches", "rural"): 573, ("fallen_branches", "wilderness"): 2364, ("iron_vein", "rural"): 76, ("old_growth", "wilderness"): 4199, ("rock_outcrop", "rural"): 229, ("tree", "rural"): 954}
-- 8396 inserted: {("fallen_branches", "rural"): 573, ("fallen_branches", "wilderness"): 2364, ("iron_vein", "rural"): 76, ("old_growth", "wilderness"): 4199, ("rock_outcrop", "rural"): 229, ("tree", "rural"): 955}

